---
const title = 'ProCode Ind';
const description =
  'ProCode Ind is an AI engineering workshop in Cartagena, Colombia. We build JATRIX and CondorPay in the open and share what we learn.';
const url = 'https://procodeind.com/';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={url} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={url} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#1e1e1e" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f6f5f4" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="64x64" href="/favicon.png" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Ubuntu:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,700;1,400;1,500&family=Ubuntu+Mono:wght@400;700&family=Ubuntu+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap"
    />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="top">
      <div class="wrap bar">
        <a class="brand" href="#home" aria-label="ProCode Ind, home">
          <span class="brand-head" id="brand-head" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="layer lines"></span><span class="layer crest"></span><span
              class="layer eye"></span>
          </span>
          <span class="brand-name">PI</span>
        </a>
        <nav class="links" aria-label="Main">
          <a href="#notebook">Notebook</a>
          <a href="#projects">Projects</a>
          <a class="hide-sm" href="#community">Community</a>
          <a class="hide-sm" href="#contact">Contact</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="home">
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="wrap hero-grid">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <span class="label"
              ><b>jespinel@procodeind</b>:<i>~</i>$ # AI engineering workshop · Cartagena, Colombia</span
            >
            <h1>We build open software and <span>share what we learn.</span></h1>
            <p class="lede">
              We work on two projects, <strong>JATRIX</strong> and <strong>CondorPay</strong>. We
              write down every decision before we code it, then publish it with its reasoning and
              its mistakes, so anyone can learn from it, use it, or make it better.
            </p>
            <div class="row">
              <a class="btn primary" href="#notebook">Read the notebook</a>
              <a class="btn" href="#community">Get involved</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <aside class="notebook" id="notebook" aria-labelledby="nb-title">
            <div class="nb-head">
              <span class="t" id="nb-title">~/notebook</span><span class="c">ls -t</span>
            </div>
            <ul class="nb-list">
              <li>
                <span class="nb-id">ADR-0012</span><span class="nb-title"
                  >Control-plane authorization</span
                ><span class="nb-st acc">accepted</span><span class="nb-proj"
                  ><span class="j">jatrix</span> · governance</span
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="nb-id">ADR-0008</span><span class="nb-title"
                  >Service-to-service authorization with a delegated subject</span
                ><span class="nb-st acc">accepted</span><span class="nb-proj"
                  ><span class="j">jatrix</span> · security</span
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="nb-id">ADR-0007</span><span class="nb-title"
                  >Asymmetric JWT signing and JWKS</span
                ><span class="nb-st pro">proposed</span><span class="nb-proj"
                  ><span class="j">jatrix</span> · identity</span
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="nb-id">ADR-0004</span><span class="nb-title"
                  >Billing and subscriptions with Wompi in Colombia</span
                ><span class="nb-st pro">proposed</span><span class="nb-proj"
                  ><span class="j">jatrix</span> · billing</span
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="nb-id">ADR-0003</span><span class="nb-title"
                  >Why v1 does not use row-level security</span
                ><span class="nb-st">decision</span><span class="nb-proj"
                  ><span class="j">jatrix</span> · data</span
                >
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="nb-id">SPEC · co</span><span class="nb-title"
                  >A Bre-B (EMVCo) QR from scratch: TLV, CRC and matrix</span
                ><span class="nb-st">spec</span><span class="nb-proj"
                  ><span class="c">condorpay</span> · payments</span
                >
              </li>
            </ul>
            <div class="nb-foot">Published on GitHub alongside each project’s code.</div>
          </aside>
          <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="iguana" id="iguana">
              <div class="part body">
                <span class="layer lines"></span><span class="layer crest"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="part tail">
                <div class="part tail-base">
                  <span class="layer lines"></span><span class="layer crest"></span>
                </div>
                <div class="part tail-tip">
                  <span class="layer lines"></span><span class="layer crest"></span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="part head">
                <span class="layer lines"></span><span class="layer crest"></span><span
                  class="layer eye"></span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="block" id="projects">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="sec-head">
            <span class="label"><i>~/projects</i>$ ls</span>
            <div>
              <h2>Two projects, documented end to end.</h2>
              <p>
                Each one solves a problem every SaaS in Latin America runs into sooner or later: who
                is allowed to do what, and how to get paid.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="projects">
            <article class="proj jatrix" aria-labelledby="p-jatrix">
              <div class="proj-top">
                <div class="proj-id">
                  <svg class="mark owl" viewBox="0 0 96 96" aria-hidden="true"
                    ><path
                      class="l"
                      d="M28 26L32 13L39 20L50 16L62 18L70 24L73 32L72 40L76 42L72 48L68 46L66 49L71 58L72 70L67 80L58 86L44 86L34 82L23 91L29 79L26 68L24 52L25 38Z"
                    ></path><path class="l" d="M42 18L46 30L52 40L62 47"></path><path
                      class="l"
                      d="M28 44L46 46L57 58L57 72L50 84L38 84L31 76L28 62Z"></path><path
                      class="l"
                      d="M31 54L52 55M30 62L56 64M31 70L56 72M34 78L52 80"></path><path
                      class="l"
                      d="M64 58L70 60M63 66L70 68M61 74L67 76"></path><path
                      class="l"
                      d="M52 86L50 91M60 85L62 91"></path><path class="l" d="M8 92H90"></path><g
                      class="eyes"
                      ><path
                        class="l"
                        d="M58.13 23L63.87 23L68 27.13L68 32.87L63.87 37L58.13 37L54 32.87L54 27.13Z"
                      ></path><path class="p" d="M59 28H63V32H59Z"></path></g
                    ></svg
                  >
                  <div>
                    <div class="proj-name" id="p-jatrix">JATRIX</div>
                    <div class="proj-kind">Governance for multi-tenant SaaS</div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="tags">
                  <span class="tag">Go</span><span class="tag">API /v1</span><span class="tag"
                    >PostgreSQL</span
                  >
                </div>
              </div>
              <p>
                Identity, organizations, tenants, per-product roles and entitlements in one service.
                Your product keeps its business logic; JATRIX decides who can do what and records
                every change.
              </p>
              <div class="learn">
                <span class="label">What you can learn here</span>
                <ul>
                  <li>How to isolate tenants in a shared schema</li>
                  <li>Per-product permissions with no inheritance and no surprises</li>
                  <li>Auditing in the same transaction as the change</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="code">
                <pre><span class="cm"># can this user do this, in this tenant, in this product?</span>
    <span class="k">POST</span> /v1/organizations/&#123;orgId&#125;/authorize</pre>
              </div>
              <div class="proj-foot">
                <a class="btn" href="https://jatrix.cloud" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                  >Documentation ↗</a
                >
              </div>
            </article>

            <article class="proj condor" aria-labelledby="p-condor">
              <div class="proj-top">
                <div class="proj-id">
                  <svg class="mark condor" viewBox="0 0 96 96" aria-hidden="true"
                    ><g class="wing wl"
                      ><path
                        class="l"
                        d="M40 40L4 33L2 37L10 40L5 43L14 45L10 49L19 49L17 54L25 52L25 58L31 54L33 59L38 54L40 52"
                      ></path><path
                        class="l"
                        d="M10 40L21 38M14 45L25 40M19 49L29 43M25 52L32 46M31 54L36 50"
                      ></path><path class="l" d="M20 36L28 41L34 47L38 52"></path></g
                    ><g class="wing wr"
                      ><path
                        class="l"
                        d="M56 40L92 33L94 37L86 40L91 43L82 45L86 49L77 49L79 54L71 52L71 58L65 54L63 59L58 54L56 52"
                      ></path><path
                        class="l"
                        d="M86 40L75 38M82 45L71 40M77 49L67 43M71 52L64 46M65 54L60 50"
                      ></path><path class="l" d="M76 36L68 41L62 47L58 52"></path></g
                    ><path class="l" d="M42 40H54L56 54L52 62H44L40 54Z"></path><path
                      class="l"
                      d="M44 62L42 72L46 70L48 74L50 70L54 72L52 62"></path><path
                      class="l"
                      d="M45 35L46 28L50 26L54 28L57 31L54 32L52 30L51 35"></path><path
                      class="a"
                      d="M40 40L42 36L44 40L46 36L48 40L50 36L52 40L54 36L56 40"></path><path
                      class="e"
                      d="M48.5 27.5H50.5V29.5H48.5Z"></path></svg
                  >
                  <div>
                    <div class="proj-name" id="p-condor">CONDORPAY</div>
                    <div class="proj-kind">Instant payments for Latin America</div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="tags">
                  <span class="tag">MIT</span><span class="tag">TypeScript</span><span class="tag"
                    >Node 20+</span
                  >
                </div>
              </div>
              <p>
                An open SDK for collecting payments over the region’s instant payment rails. It
                starts in Colombia with Bre-B QR codes and Wompi, and plugs into Medusa.
              </p>
              <table class="pkgs" aria-label="Packages published on npm">
                <tbody>
                  <tr><td>@condorpay/sdk</td><td>0.1.6</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>@condorpay/co</td><td>0.3.0</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>@condorpay/medusa</td><td>2.0.0</td></tr>
                  <tr
                    ><td class="soon">Brazil · Mexico · United States</td><td class="soon"
                      >in progress</td
                    ></tr
                  >
                </tbody>
              </table>
              <div class="code">
                <pre><span class="k">import</span> &#123; CondorPay &#125; <span class="k">from</span> <span class="s">"@condorpay/sdk"</span>;

    <span class="k">const</span> cp = <span class="k">new</span> CondorPay(&#123; country: <span class="s">"co"</span>, wompi: &#123; publicKey, privateKey &#125; &#125;);
    <span class="k">const</span> qr = cp.co.generateQr(&#123; merchantName: <span class="s">"My Store"</span>, merchantCity: <span class="s">"Cartagena"</span>, merchantAccountId &#125;);</pre>
              </div>
              <div class="proj-foot">
                <div class="copyrow" style="flex:1">
                  <code id="npm-cmd">npm install @condorpay/sdk</code>
                  <button type="button" data-copy="npm-cmd">Copy</button>
                </div>
                <a
                  class="btn"
                  href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@condorpay/sdk"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener">npm ↗</a
                >
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="block" aria-labelledby="pr-title">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="sec-head">
            <span class="label"><i>~/rules</i>$ cat PRINCIPLES.md</span>
            <div>
              <h2 id="pr-title">Six rules we apply to everything we make.</h2>
              <p>
                They are written into each project’s specification. If a rule changes, the document
                changes first.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="principles">
            <div class="pr">
              <span class="k">spec → code</span><h3>Write it down, then build it</h3><p>
                Every structural change goes through an ADR. The specification is the source of
                truth.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="pr">
              <span class="k">tenant_id</span><h3>Isolation by default</h3><p>
                Every query filters by organization and tenant. Context comes from the token, never
                from the request body.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="pr">
              <span class="k">audit_log</span><h3>Everything leaves a trail</h3><p>
                Every state change is recorded in the same transaction that makes it.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="pr">
              <span class="k">OpenTelemetry</span><h3>Everything is observable</h3><p>
                Every signal carries organization, tenant, product, user and request_id.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="pr">
              <span class="k">/v1 → /v2</span><h3>Nothing breaks quietly</h3><p>
                A breaking change is a new API version.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="pr">
              <span class="k">cost-aware</span><h3>Only what is needed</h3><p>
                A shared schema, stateless compute, and no infrastructure before it is needed.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="block" id="community" aria-labelledby="com-title">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="sec-head">
            <span class="label"><i>~/community</i>$ cat CONTRIBUTING.md</span>
            <div>
              <h2 id="com-title">
                There is room for you, whether you know a lot or are just starting.
              </h2>
              <p>
                Conversations happen in public, in English or Spanish. The rules for taking part are
                written down and the same for everyone.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ways">
            <div class="way">
              <span class="k">read</span><h3>Learn from the decisions</h3><p>
                Each ADR explains the problem, the options, and why we chose one.
              </p><a href="#notebook">Go to the notebook →</a>
            </div>
            <div class="way">
              <span class="k">ask</span><h3>Start a discussion</h3><p>
                Questions, ideas, or a better way to do it. We answer in public so it helps others
                too.
              </p><a href="https://github.com/procode-ind" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >GitHub ↗</a
              >
            </div>
            <div class="way">
              <span class="k">contribute</span><h3>Send your first change</h3><p>
                Some issues are labeled good first issue. Just sign off your commits with <code
                  >git commit -s</code
                >.
              </p><a href="https://github.com/procode-ind" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >See issues ↗</a
              >
            </div>
            <div class="way">
              <span class="k">sustain</span><h3>Sponsor the work</h3><p>
                Your support pays for maintainer time, CI, and security audits.
              </p><a href="https://github.com/sponsors/procode-ind" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >Sponsor ↗</a
              >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="block" aria-labelledby="f-title">
        <div class="wrap founder">
          <div class="card">
            <div class="mono-av" aria-hidden="true">JE</div>
            <div>
              <div class="nm" id="f-title">Jeffrey Espinel</div>
              <div class="rl">AI software engineer · founder</div>
            </div>
            <p class="rl">Cartagena, Colombia</p>
          </div>
          <div class="letter">
            <p>
              I started ProCode Ind to build the infrastructure I kept rebuilding on every project:
              multi-tenant governance and payments for Latin America.
            </p>
            <p>
              I chose to do it in the open. What I learn designing these systems should not stay in
              a private repository.
            </p>
            <p class="small">
              I run the company with a team of AI agents versioned as code, covering planning,
              finance and maintenance. That system will be open too.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="contact" id="contact">
        <div class="wrap contact-in">
          <div>
            <span class="label"><i>~/contact</i>$ mail</span>
            <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Write to us.</h2>
            <p>
              For questions about JATRIX or CondorPay, sponsorships, or if you want to build with
              us.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="copyrow">
              <code id="mail">jespinel@procodeind.com</code>
              <button type="button" data-copy="mail">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <p class="small-note">
              Security reports: same address, with [SECURITY] in the subject.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <div class="wrap foot">
        <span>© 2026 ProCode Ind LLC · Cartagena, Colombia</span>
        <span
          ><a href="https://jatrix.cloud" target="_blank" rel="noopener">JATRIX</a> · <a
            href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@condorpay/sdk"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">CondorPay</a
          > · <a href="https://github.com/procode-ind" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a
          ></span
        >
      </div>
    </footer>
    <script is:inline src="/assets/site.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
